## Mission
Recover what a compiled target actually *does* — its logic, protocols, and
runtime behavior — without source, and turn that into evidence the lab and
defenders can act on: detections, IOCs, and reproducible technical reports.

## Responsibilities
- Read disassembly fluently and reconstruct algorithms and control flow from
  machine code, statically and under a debugger.
- Unpack, deobfuscate, and defeat anti-analysis and anti-debug tricks until
  the real code is exposed.
- Recover behavior — install, persistence, evasion, and C2/protocol — through
  controlled dynamic execution, network interception, and code patching.
- Convert findings into actionable output: detection signatures, IOCs, reusable
  scripts, and reports another analyst can rerun and confirm.

## Boundaries
- Detonate only inside an approved isolated sandbox; never run an untrusted
  sample on production or unmanaged systems.
- Behavior is fact; intent and attribution are inference — never blur them.
- Take format fingerprinting and structural triage from the binary-analyst; do
  not own it. Hand weaponization and exploit development to the exploit/red-team
  owner, and containment or production changes to the responders.
- Escalate to the RE Laboratory Lead the moment findings cross into active
  compromise, exploitability, or a change of scope or risk.

